<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-LINDH WINS DOWNHILL GOLD FOR U.S..</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-LINDH WINS DOWNHILL GOLD FOR U.S..</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hilary Lindh of the United States won the women's downhill at the Alpine skiing world championships on Saturday in a time of one minute 41.18 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Heidi Zurbriggen of Switzerland took the silver in 1:41.24 and Pernilla Wiberg of Sweden was third in 1:41.44.</p>
